#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119567 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "ba897e22-8104-5772-a0d3-9b062f3592f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4932" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(-3,2,1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 0, 2, 0 \\rangle$." :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,1 \\rangle\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 0,2,0 \\rangle\n$$\n\nis normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{r} - \\mathbf{p}) \\cdot \\mathbf{n} = 0\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $\\mathbf p$ is the position vector of $P$.\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(r - p) \\cdot n &= 0 \\\\\nr \\cdot n - p \\cdot n &= 0 \\\\\nr \\cdot n &= p \\cdot n \\\\\nr \\cdot ⟨0, 2, 0⟩ &= ⟨ - 3, 2, 1⟩ \\cdot ⟨0, 2, 0⟩ \\\\\nr \\cdot ⟨0, 2, 0⟩ &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119568 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "a33f6c43-4e25-5d67-9f73-ca99a18fb434" :question/math-academy-id "e-4933" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $\\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{b}, \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{c} \\rangle$ is parallel to the plane $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle = 3$. What is the value of $\\dfrac{b}{c}$?" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle t_1,t_2,t_3 \\rangle\n$$\n\nthat is parallel to the given plane.\n\nFrom the equation\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle = 3\n$$\n\nof the plane, we get the normal vector\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle\n$$\n\nSo, $\\mathbf{v} \\perp \\mathbf{n}$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv \\cdot n &= 0 \\\\\n⟨t_{1}, t_{2}, t_{3}⟩ \\cdot ⟨2,-1, 4⟩ &= 0 \\\\\n2t_{1} - t_{2} + 4t_{3} &= 0 \\\\\nt_{2} &= 2t_{1} + 4t_{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v}=\\langle t_1, 2t_1 + 4t_3, t_3 \\rangle\n$$\n\nwhere $t_1,t_3 \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nWe are told that the first component of $\\mathbf{v}$ equals $0$. So, we must set $t_1=0$.\n\nSince $\\mathbf{v}$ is nonzero, we can pick any\n\n$$\nt_3 \\neq 0\n$$\n\nFor example, setting $t_3=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{4}, \\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{1} \\rangle\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{b}{c} = 4\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119569 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/id #uuid "43586a83-879c-5caf-9063-a8f4afbb8b4c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4935" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(\\sqrt{2},0,-5)$ and is perpendicular to the line\n${x = 3; y =-1 + \\sqrt{3}t; z = 5 - t$." :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{q}=\\langle \\sqrt{2},0,-5 \\rangle\n$$\n\nConverting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{x = 3; y =-1 + \\sqrt{3}t; z = 5 - t\n$$\n\nThe direction vector of the line is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v}=\\langle 0, \\sqrt{3}, -1\\rangle\n$$\n\nso a normal vector to the plane is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\mathbf{v}=\\langle 0, \\sqrt{3}, -1 \\rangle\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(r - q) \\cdot n &= 0 \\\\\nr \\cdot n - q \\cdot n &= 0 \\\\\nr \\cdot n &= q \\cdot n \\\\\nr \\cdot ⟨0, \\sqrt{3},-1⟩ &= ⟨\\sqrt{2}, 0,-5⟩ \\cdot ⟨0, \\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\\nr \\cdot ⟨0, \\sqrt{3},-1⟩ &= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4bff29e-8a55-5152-bd5e-c28937dbd187" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119086} {:answer/id #uuid "c406bae9-4652-564b-8df2-406d995a5d35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119087} {:answer/id #uuid "c5e667c5-21b7-59a1-b4ad-12b289d841d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119088} {:answer/id #uuid "168f6906-cead-5d6d-9a98-9eb3f88fa6f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119089} {:answer/id #uuid "6b0659b9-afa6-5125-833a-15bb73ab7574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119090}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b0659b9-afa6-5125-833a-15bb73ab7574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119090} :answer-field/id #uuid "b2c9baab-9c48-5d09-ac05-3fd6629fd144" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186119085}] :question/id #uuid "f1725487-2c6d-5d22-95bb-183dbe4038eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-70821" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $⟨a, 0, c⟩$ is parallel to the plane $r \\cdot ⟨3,-3, 1⟩ =-12$. What is the value of $\\frac{a}{c}$?"}]}
